# Bug Registry Workflow (Mandatory)

When the user reports a bug/regression:

1. Read `doc/BUGS.md` before implementing fixes.
2. Search for related entries by `keywords`/symptom.
3. Reuse proven fixes/guards when applicable.
4. If bug is new, add a new entry to `doc/BUGS.md` (newest first) using the template.
5. If bug already exists, update its status and `Fix`/`Guards/tests` fields.
6. For substantial fixes, also add an entry to `doc/ENGINEERING_NOTES.md`.
7. During active bug resolution, every newly observed symptom/error message must be appended to the related bug entry immediately (same session), not deferred.
8. If a fix attempt reveals a second root cause, update `Root cause` and set status to `partially fixed` until user confirms end-to-end behavior.

Before finishing bug-related work:

- Confirm whether issue is `fixed` vs `partially fixed`.
- Explicitly list residual risks/testing gaps.
- Avoid heuristic/fallback-first implementations when session/source-of-truth data exists.

